WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.299 --> 00:00:16.802
danced and shouted but couldn't pry the baby monkey from his shoulders.

2
00:00:16.822 --> 00:00:18.583
"Stand still," I said.

3
00:00:18.603 --> 00:00:19.884
"You're only upsetting him."

4
00:00:20.565 --> 00:00:24.028
I pulled out a biscuit and offered a piece to the monkey, who was no bigger than a

5
00:00:24.068 --> 00:00:29.472
kitten. Finally after some coaxing, I was able to take the monkey into my own arms.

6
00:00:29.492 --> 00:00:32.395
"What a cute little fellow he is!"

7
00:00:32.855 --> 00:00:33.656
exclaimed Fritz.

8
00:00:34.476 --> 00:00:35.777
"Do let me keep him, Father.

9
00:00:36.097 --> 00:00:37.198
I'll call him Knips."

10
00:00:37.998 --> 00:00:44.242
The monkey settled himself on Fritz's shoulder—calmly this time—and I helped to carry Fritz's sugarcane.

11
00:00:45.383 --> 00:00:48.825
But Knips soon scrambled into Fritz's arms, which were already full.

12
00:00:49.545 --> 00:00:50.126
"Come, Turk!"

13
00:00:50.426 --> 00:00:53.127
Fritz called, and the dog came quickly to his side.

14
00:00:53.147 --> 00:00:56.049
"Now I need you to be a good dog."

15
00:00:56.810 --> 00:01:00.432
Fritz seated Knips on Turk's back and secured the monkey with a cord.

16
00:01:01.036 --> 00:01:04.579
Then he put a second cord around Turk's neck so he could lead the dog.

17
00:01:05.839 --> 00:01:09.742
At first neither animal was pleased with this arrangement, but they soon got used to it.

18
00:01:12.004 --> 00:01:15.106
We made our way back to camp, where my wife was preparing supper.

19
00:01:15.126 --> 00:01:17.728
"A monkey!

20
00:01:17.748 --> 00:01:18.989
A monkey!"

21
00:01:19.229 --> 00:01:21.150
cried Franz as he spied the new pet.

22
00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:22.891
"Where did you find him?"

23
00:01:23.171 --> 00:01:23.792
asked Ernest.

24
00:01:24.993 --> 00:01:27.214
"Why are you carrying a bundle of sticks?

25
00:01:27.935 --> 00:01:29.336
What are those strange nuts?"

26
00:01:29.992 --> 00:01:32.773
said Jack as he caught sight of the sugarcane and coconuts.

27
00:01:33.914 --> 00:01:36.115
Over our meal we answered all their questions.

28
00:01:36.995 --> 00:01:42.117
Although Fritz tried to feed Knips, the monkey was not interested in our meal of fish and cheese.

29
00:01:42.877 --> 00:01:47.019
But I persuaded Knips to suck liquid from a handkerchief that had been dipped in a coconut.

30
00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:53.642
The next morning I decided that Fritz and I should return to the wreck.

31
00:01:54.422 --> 00:02:00.528
Since the ship was meant to supply a colony, there were still many useful things onboard.

32
00:02:00.548 --> 00:02:04.830
I wanted to retrieve them before a storm damaged the wreck, and I wanted to check on the

33
00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:08.151
animals. Fritz insisted on taking Knips along.

34
00:02:16.315 --> 00:02:19.416
When we boarded the ship, the animals seemed glad to see us.

35
00:02:20.557 --> 00:02:24.558
We checked that they had enough food and then began examining the contents of the ship.

36
00:02:25.359 --> 00:02:30.412
We loaded some food and supplies onto our tub boat, but I kept thinking about the animals.

37
00:02:31.393 --> 00:02:34.053
"Fritz, I'm beginning to feel sorry for these poor creatures.

38
00:02:34.974 --> 00:02:37.895
I wish there were some way we could get them all ashore."

39
00:02:37.915 --> 00:02:42.616
"We could make a raft and take one or two at a time," he suggested.

40
00:02:42.636 --> 00:02:48.918
"It's easy enough to say 'make a raft,' but it's quite another thing to actually make one," I

41
00:02:48.978 --> 00:02:49.498
pointed out.

42
00:02:50.318 --> 00:02:52.059
"Well, I can't think of anything else."

43
00:02:52.459 --> 00:02:53.119
Fritz frowned.

44
00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:57.100
"Unless we make them life preservers like we made for ourselves."

45
00:02:58.448 --> 00:02:59.429
"That's a good idea!"

46
00:02:59.749 --> 00:03:00.330
I exclaimed.

47
00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:02.031
Fritz started to laugh.

48
00:03:02.051 --> 00:03:04.733
"Really, my boy, I'm not joking.

49
00:03:05.433 --> 00:03:08.075
We could probably get all the animals ashore that way."

50
00:03:08.856 --> 00:03:12.158
So I found a fat sheep and began to put our plan into action.

51
00:03:13.299 --> 00:03:15.981
First I fastened a wide piece of linen around its belly.

52
00:03:16.762 --> 00:03:19.884
Next I attached some corks and empty tins to the linen.

53
00:03:20.605 --> 00:03:23.507
Then, with Fritz's help, I dropped the animal into the sea.

54
00:03:24.347 --> 00:03:24.828
It sank!

55
00:03:25.868 --> 00:03:28.749
But a moment later, it rose to the surface and floated perfectly.

56
00:03:28.769 --> 00:03:31.450
"Hurrah!" exclaimed Fritz.

57
00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:34.452
"We'll make life preservers for all the animals!"

58
00:03:35.292 --> 00:03:38.993
We then quickly caught the other animals and provided them with similar devices.

59
00:03:39.834 --> 00:03:44.356
The cow and the donkey gave us more trouble than the others because we needed something more buoyant

60
00:03:44.416 --> 00:03:45.876
than cork to help them float.

61
00:03:46.877 --> 00:03:50.498
But at last we found some empty casks and fastened two to each animal.

62
00:03:53.039 --> 00:03:56.813
The whole herd was now ready to start, and the donkey was the first to be launched.

63
00:04:00.413 --> 00:04:05.295
After some maneuvering, we got him into a good position, and then heaved him into the water.

64
00:04:06.375 --> 00:04:09.536
Like the sheep, he sank but immediately surfaced again.

65
00:04:10.616 --> 00:04:16.778
The cow, sheep, and goats followed him, one after another, until only the pig remained.

66
00:04:17.478 --> 00:04:19.559
But she seemed determined not to leave the ship.

67
00:04:20.279 --> 00:04:24.400
She kicked and squealed so violently that I really thought we would have to abandon her.

68
00:04:25.452 --> 00:04:28.574
Finally after much trouble, we succeeded in launching her.

69
00:04:29.354 --> 00:04:32.216
We had fastened a rope to the neck or horns of each animal.

70
00:04:34.678 --> 00:04:36.659
Ready to embark, we gathered up the ropes.

71
00:04:37.519 --> 00:04:40.101
Then we set sail, pulling our herd behind us.

72
00:04:40.981 --> 00:04:44.804
Delighted with the success of our plan, we got out some biscuits for lunch.

73
00:04:48.526 --> 00:04:51.928
While Fritz amused himself with Knips, I took out my telescope.

74
00:04:52.828 --> 00:04:56.914
I was trying to see what our loved ones were doing onshore when Fritz suddenly shouted.

75
00:04:56.934 --> 00:04:59.078
"Shark!" he cried.

76
00:04:59.819 --> 00:05:02.823
A huge shark was headed straight for one of our finest sheep.
